  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 300 AM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nTuesday through Saturday...With the flattening ridge transition, the \nlocal area may be under the battle zone of the LLVL thermal gradient \nand upper level short wave propagation path for almost daily chance \nof showers and storms for much of the week and even into the \nweekend. This deep summer-like MCS-track for much of the week from \nthe central plains over to the southern GRT LKS and OH RVR Valley \nmay add up to quite a bit of rainfall by Friday. At least temps look \ncooler by late week and into the weekend as well, with a day or two \npossibly held down in the 70s with cloud cover and east winds.",
